    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (257 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response is an `OwnerDto` generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by `OwnerMapper` (MapStruct). The `membershipTier` field is a derived, read-only field, following the same pattern as the existing derived fields (`displayName`, `membershipNumber`, etc.), so I added it in two places:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(formatMembershipTier(owner))\")` plus a `formatMembershipTier` helper implementing the rule: returns `\"SILVER\"` when `namesakeCount == 0` **and** an email is present, otherwise `\"BRONZE\"`.\n\nThe `namesakeCount` is already computed and stored at owner-creation time in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, and email is stored (lower-cased) on the same path, so both inputs are available when the DTO is mapped for the GET response.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass, and no existing tests regressed.",
